---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Hybrid Manufacturing"
  description="ARMS researches CNC machining and directed energy deposition hybrid manufacturing."
  current="/research/hybrid-manufacturing/"
>
  <section class="section detail-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research / Hybrid manufacturing</p>
    <h1>
      Connecting deposition
      <br />
      and machining.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We investigate how CNC machining and directed energy deposition can be
      combined to build and finish parts, linking process planning, deposition
      control, and experimental measurement.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img
        class="detail-photo"
        src="/images/hybrid-cover.webp"
        width="1067"
        height="711"
        alt="LT65 setup with laser deposition head and monitoring instrumentation"
      />
      <figcaption>LT65 hybrid manufacturing setup.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft">
    <p class="eyebrow">Explore the research</p>
    <h2>Study the process. Examine the part.</h2>
    <nav
      class="project-nav"
      aria-label="Hybrid manufacturing research examples"
    >
      <a href="#grid-molding">
        01 / Grid molding <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#ded-control">
        02 / DED process control <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#process-planning">
        03 / Process selection <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
    </nav>
    <div class="three">
      <div>
        <h3>Process planning</h3>
        <p>
          Investigate the relationship between material addition and material
          removal.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Deposition control</h3>
        <p>Explore how process decisions affect the deposited material.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Experimental measurement</h3>
        <p>Use instrumented experiments to examine process behavior.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="grid-molding">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example research / Grid molding</p>
    <h2 class="grid-heading">
      Conformal grid plastic injection mold fabricated by machining/DED hybrid
      manufacturing
    </h2>
    <div class="grid-overview">
      <p>
        Prepared blocks are assembled into an approximate mold body. Directed
        energy deposition then forms a continuous surface over the blocks,
        followed by finish milling to produce the final geometry. The hybrid
        process incorporates a three-dimensional cooling grid. After optimizing
        the design, ARMS fabricated a prototype and compared it with molds
        produced by other methods; the cooling grid delivered a significant
        improvement in cooling performance.
      </p>
      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/grid-mold.webp"
          width="1800"
          height="1200"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="Conformal grid plastic injection mold with two machined cavities"
        />
        <figcaption>Conformal grid plastic injection mold.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <div
        class="diagram-scroll"
        tabindex="0"
        role="region"
        aria-label="Grid molding process diagram; scroll horizontally to inspect on small screens"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/grid-process.webp"
          width="1800"
          height="483"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="Grid molding sequence showing prepared blocks, a three-dimensional cooling grid, and the final deposited and machined mold surface"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Grid molding technique: prepared blocks, a three-dimensional cooling
        grid, and the deposited and machined mold surface.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft" id="ded-control">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example research / DED process control</p>
    <h2>
      Adaptive, Productive, and Quality (APQ) control for directed energy
      deposition
    </h2>
    <p>
      ARMS is developing an integrated DED process control system that combines
      monitoring of deposition height, width, and temperature with coordinated
      regulation of energy fluence and powder fluence. An in-house Dynamic
      Powder Splitting System (DPSS) enables powder delivery control within this
      framework. The research aims to coordinate deposition geometry and thermal
      conditions while addressing productivity and part quality.
    </p>
    <figure class="wide-figure">
      <img
        class="apq-diagram"
        src="/images/apq-control-lossless.webp"
        width="1200"
        height="671"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="APQ control system linking temperature, deposition height, and width measurements to energy and geometry control modules and powder delivery through the DPSS"
      />
      <figcaption>
        APQ DED control architecture, integrating monitoring, energy control,
        and DPSS-based powder delivery.
        <a class="figure-enlarge" href="/images/apq-control-lossless.webp">
          Open full-size control diagram ↗
        </a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="process-planning">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example research / Process planning</p>
    <h2>Decision-support software for machining/DED process selection</h2>
    <p>
      Choosing how to produce a part on a machining/DED hybrid machine tool
      requires comparing three strategies: machining alone, DED alone, or an
      integrated hybrid route. This decision typically depends on specialized
      process knowledge and detailed, time-intensive planning. ARMS
      process-selection software evaluates candidate routes and helps users
      identify a preferred manufacturing approach based on productivity,
      material cost, and energy consumption.
    </p>
    <figure class="wide-figure">
      <img
        src="/images/process-selection.webp"
        width="1800"
        height="1014"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="ARMS process-selection software showing a component decomposed into features for machining, DED, or hybrid manufacturing analysis"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Process-selection software for evaluating machining, DED, and hybrid
        manufacturing routes.
        <a class="figure-enlarge" href="/images/process-selection.webp">
          Open full-size software figure ↗
        </a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
